Package: bilatr
Title: Hierarchical Dynamic IRT Models for Dyadic Conflict Trajectories
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("David", "Randahl", , "david.randahl@fhs.se", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Magnus", "Lundgren", role = "aut"),
    person("Carl", "Vikberg", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Fits a hierarchical Bayesian dynamic item-response-theory-style
    model to dyadic event data (GDELT/ICEWS, CAMEO-coded) in order to
    estimate latent conflict trajectories. Action types discriminate
    between high- and low-conflict states through a Dirichlet-multinomial
    likelihood, and dyad-specific latent states follow a random-walk
    process, with support for both single-dyad time-series and
    multi-dyad panel estimation. Includes GDELT/ICEWS ingestion and
    CAMEO recoding helpers, 'cmdstanr'-based fitting wrappers, and tidy
    posterior extraction utilities.
